   "source": [
    "# BRISC2025 Tissue-Mask Kernel Training (Structured + Single Radial)\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook keeps the same approach as `radial_single_kernel_fi_optimization.ipynb`, but adds two stages upfront for BRISC2025:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Build train/val/test patch folders from `data_brain/brisc2025/segmentation_task` where **mask pixels are tumor**.\n",
    "2. Run the structured multi-kernel pipeline (same MMR/composite setup as `kernel_model_structured`) to produce `composite_kernel.npy`.\n",
    "3. Continue with single-kernel radial `f(r)` optimization and evaluation using that composite kernel.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "bb9a28bf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
